{%- doc -%}
  Prints the trade discount percentage (an integer) that applies to a product for the
  logged-in customer, or 0 when the customer is not an approved trade account.

  Approved trade customers carry the tag set in Theme settings → ETS trade pricing
  (default "trade"). The product's band comes from the product metafield
  `ets.trade_band` (0, 5, 10, 15, 20 or 25), which mirrors the manual collection
  `trade-list-N` the product sits in. The "Trade price – N%" automatic discounts on those
  collections take the same percentage off in the cart, so what the page shows is what
  the customer pays. Pricing rules: store-content/pricing/PRICING-PLAYBOOK.md.

  Usage: {%- capture pct -%}{% render 'ets-trade-rate', product: product %}{%- endcapture -%}
  @param {product} product
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- liquid
  assign pct = 0
  assign trade_tag = settings.ets_trade_tag | default: 'trade' | strip
  if customer and settings.ets_trade_enabled and product != blank
    if customer.tags contains trade_tag
      assign band = product.metafields.ets.trade_band.value | default: 0 | plus: 0
      if band >= 5 and band <= 25
        assign pct = band
      endif
    endif
  endif
  echo pct | default: 0
-%}
